# Evidence captures are live output from the running app — real card text, real
# mail subjects, real session prompts, real PR titles. The QA_EVIDENCE set
# already committed is deliberate; new ones are not, and a `git add -A` swept a
# whole run in once without anyone looking at it.
#
# Matched as a family rather than by name because the second one to appear was
# called IA_EVIDENCE, an hour later, mid-capture. `git add -f` to include one on
# purpose.
*_EVIDENCE/

# Working prompts and briefs. Same reason as the evidence directories above:
# they quote real card titles, real session prompts and real mail subjects
# verbatim, and they name the operator's live Truto profiles by count. They are
# working documents, not shipped ones.
#
# `OPUS_ULTRATHINK.PROMPT.md` reached the repository through a `git add -A` in
# this session — the exact sweep the rule above was written about — and is
# removed from tracking here rather than left in.
detailed.md
*.PROMPT.md
# The same documents under the other name they arrive with. `*.PROMPT.md` was
# written against one session's filename and misses `CLAUDE_PROMPT_OVERHAUL.md`
# and `CLAUDE_PROMPT_THREADS.md` by a single underscore -- both sat untracked
# and one `git add -A` away from carrying real Slack titles and mail subjects
# into a public repository. The rule is about what the file contains, so the
# pattern matches on that rather than on how a given session happened to name it.
CLAUDE_PROMPT*.md
